hub.com/users/rbdixon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-19T15:21:11Z","updated_at":"2021-11-19T15:21:11Z","body":"It took a little digging but the issue is that the `mitmproxy.controller.DummyReply` instance can not be pickled. This is required for copying the object which is done when presenting the overlay.\r\n\r\nI added a `__deepcopy__(self, memo)` method to `DummyReply` which seems like a fix. I'm not exactly sure what I'm doing down in this area of code so if someone wants to review this and approves I'll send a PR:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n    def __deepcopy__(self, memo):\r\n        cls = self.__class__\r\n        result = cls.__new__(cls)\r\n        memo[id(self)] = result\r\n        result._state = self._state\r\n        result._should_reset = self._should_reset\r\n        return result\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/comments/974162749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rbdixon","id":35279,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Mjc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon","html_url":"https://github.com/rbdixon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rbdixon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r